  "model": "Kokoro-82M v1.0 ONNX (onnx-community, Apache-2.0)",
  "lines": [
    {
      "id": "l01",
      "text": "Leave the fridge open on a hot day, and the kitchen gets warmer.",
      "file": "l01.wav",
      "duration": 3.625,
      "sr": 24000,
      "words_per_s": 3.59
    },
    {
      "id": "l02",
      "text": "So how can a cold box heat a room?",
      "file": "l02.wav",
      "duration": 1.826,
      "sr": 24000,
      "words_per_s": 4.93
    },
    {
      "id": "l03",
      "text": "A fridge doesn't make cold. It pumps heat.",
      "file": "l03.wav",
      "duration": 2.456,
      "sr": 24000,
      "words_per_s": 3.26
    },
    {
      "id": "l04",
      "text": "Cold fluid in the inside coils evaporates, soaking up your food's heat.",
      "file": "l04.wav",
      "duration": 4.26,
      "sr": 24000,
      "words_per_s": 2.82
    },
    {
      "id": "l05",
      "text": "A compressor squeezes it hotter than the room, and coils outside the box release that heat.",
      "file": "l05.wav",
      "duration": 4.965,
      "sr": 24000,
      "words_per_s": 3.22
    },
    {
      "id": "l06",
      "text": "Door open, that heat just circles back, plus the motor's own.",
      "file": "l06.wav",
      "duration": 3.479,
      "sr": 24000,
      "words_per_s": 3.16
    },
    {
      "id": "l07",
      "text": "That's why air conditioners dump their heat outdoors.",
      "file": "l07.wav",
      "duration": 2.735,
      "sr": 24000,
      "words_per_s": 2.93
    },
    {
      "id": "l08",
      "text": "Download Recall to turn your study material into lessons.",
      "file": "l08.wav",
      "duration": 3.283,
      "sr": 24000,
      "words_per_s": 2.74
    }
  ]
}